Better: restore the previous producer edges on error. `resetProducers()` clears edges. Before resetting, capture the current edges; on throw, restore them. But the effect records new producers DURING fn.run() (via ReactiveContext). On throw, some new producers were added. The old producers are gone (reset). To restore "the effect subscribes to its signals so it re-fires on the next change," I could:
