The cleanest correct fix: capture the producer set before reset; on error, restore the captured set (so the effect remains subscribed to its OLD dependencies) and re-mark dirty (so it retries immediately on the next flush). If the effect was reading a NEW signal when it threw, it won't track that new one until it runs successfully — but it'll retry on the next change of its OLD deps, and once it runs cleanly, it records the correct deps. That's acceptable and safe.

Let me look at ReactiveNode to see how to capture/restore producers. Let me read it.

### 3. Transport-level PONG

Quarkus PathlandSocket.onBinary:
