// `minmax(0,1fr)` (not bare `1fr`): a bare `1fr` track has an
                // implicit `minmax(auto,1fr)` minimum equal to the largest
                // child's min-content size, so a short viewport can't shrink the
                // ZStack and its `end`-aligned child (e.g. a player bar) is
                // pushed out of view. `minmax(0,1fr)` lets the track shrink and
                // the inner ScrollView take over. A Hug ZStack is unaffected —
                // in an indefinite (max-content) container `1fr` still resolves
                // to max-content.
